The MJCF and its 18 referenced meshes are copied without modification.
Unused meshes, the standalone scene, images and upstream development files
are excluded. MuJoCo Menagerie derives the model from The Robot Studio:
https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100/tree/main/Simulation/SO101

Joint names and positions follow this MJCF calibration. Positions are radians;
they are not LeRobot's normalized hardware actions or servo register values.
The source gripperframe site defines the TCP position used by RobotSpec.
RobotSpec retains the gripper body's orientation as its TCP orientation.

SO-101 leader acquisition handle model

Source: https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100/tree/a758567c3978dfeefe282ede0500085a48fe8f78/Simulation/SO101
Revision: a758567c3978dfeefe282ede0500085a48fe8f78
License: Apache-2.0; see LICENSE in this directory.
so101_leader_new_calib.urdf and Handle_SO101.stl, Trigger_SO101.stl,
Wrist_Roll_SO101.stl are upstream copies. so101_leader.xml adapts the
leader head subtree to the canonical follower arm; scene_leader.xml supplies a floor.
The upstream trigger travel (0-45 degrees) is a provisional CAD estimate.
Our adapted joint/actuator range is 0-30 degrees, confirmed by the user for
arm1 on 2026-10-11 with independent 0/15/30-degree encoder alignment.
Printed-part inertias remain upstream CAD estimates. The gripperframe
site remains a follower compatibility frame, not the physical leader tool tip.
Canonical so101.xml and the original 18 meshes remain unchanged.
